(7695727, 1261841, 68504, '<td valign="top">great comings and goings, in and out of the mist.</td>', 'great comings and goings, in and out of the mist.', '2021-06-09 00:47:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(7695730, 1261938, 67145, '<td valign="top">this is so dramatic and so full of atmosphere .. <br/>it seems more a mixture of low contrast and high contrast .. just because of the difference between the darker bits of the trees and the beautiful soft background and lighter trees .. <br/>but that''s just my opinion and i''m not an authority .. <br/>i''m glad this got the blue .. because it really is stunning .. <br/>its one of those images that will remain in my memory for a long time .. <br/>like a wonderful song .. <br/>oh .. btw .. CONGRATULATIONS on the blue .. :)</td>', 'this is so dramatic and so full of atmosphere .. it seems more a mixture of low contrast and high contrast .. just because of the difference between the darker bits of the trees and the beautiful soft background and lighter trees .. but that''s just my opinion and i''m not an authority .. i''m glad this got the blue .. because it really is stunning .. its one of those images that will remain in my memory for a long time .. like a wonderful song .. oh .. btw .. CONGRATULATIONS on the blue .. :)', '2021-06-09 01:07:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(7695733, 1261822, 68504, '<td valign="top">undersung. lovely natural low contrast, naturally muted colours. good lines: we slope into umbrella lady and join her up the road to wherever...</td>', 'undersung. lovely natural low contrast, naturally muted colours. good lines: we slope into umbrella lady and join her up the road to wherever...', '2021-06-09 01:18:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(7695734, 1261719, 68504, '<td valign="top">you goof! will gardening happen?</td>', 'you goof! will gardening happen?', '2021-06-09 01:21:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(7695737, 1261956, 50641, '<td valign="top">Oh so glowy!</td>', 'Oh so glowy!', '2021-06-09 02:58:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(7695740, 1261774, 182539, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by willem:</b></div><hr/><i> I don''t like the effect applied and it is not low contrast in my view. The tones are evenly and widely distributed in the histogram, except for the real/almost black and real/almost white. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yep, realised too late that I submitted the wrong photo re effect. I learnt a bit about histograms now. Thanks!</td>', 'Originally posted by willem: I don''t like the effect applied and it is not low contrast in my view. The tones are evenly and widely distributed in the histogram, except for the real/almost black and real/almost white.   Yep, realised too late that I submitted the wrong photo re effect. I learnt a bit about histograms now. Thanks!', '2021-06-09 04:43:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(7695743, 1261936, 67145, '<td valign="top">this is stunning .. <br/>I''m looking at it on my phone so I''m not getting the full impact .. will definitely check it out on computer tomorrow .. <br/>the mist .. <br/>the atmosphere  .. <br/>the feeling that I could hear a pin drop ..<br/> <br/>I''m no expert but this looks like low contrast to me .. brilliant  .. :)<br/></td>', 'this is stunning .. I''m looking at it on my phone so I''m not getting the full impact .. will definitely check it out on computer tomorrow .. the mist .. the atmosphere  .. the feeling that I could hear a pin drop .. I''m no expert but this looks like low contrast to me .. brilliant  .. :)', '2021-06-09 08:39:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(7695745, 1261840, 97225, '<td valign="top">This is really lovely. I was your 10.</td>', 'This is really lovely. I was your 10.', '2021-06-09 09:42:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(7695748, 1261672, 100831, '<td valign="top">All is calm!  Looking at this I understand how you thought my entry was not low contrast. To me, lack of shadows (there are certainly none here) and any contrast in lighting is key. But I think low contrast can still include a subject.</td>', 'All is calm!  Looking at this I understand how you thought my entry was not low contrast. To me, lack of shadows (there are certainly none here) and any contrast in lighting is key. But I think low contrast can still include a subject.', '2021-06-09 10:15:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(7695755, 1261942, 4008, '<td valign="top">Just to add: I still rated your image as a low contrast image, compliant with the challenge, because it feels low contrast and does not rely on the contrast between dark and light tones, but instead shows a subtle combination of soft colors.</td>', 'Just to add: I still rated your image as a low contrast image, compliant with the challenge, because it feels low contrast and does not rely on the contrast between dark and light tones, but instead shows a subtle combination of soft colors.', '2021-06-09 11:46:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(7695757, 1261672, 4008, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by PennyStreet:</b></div><hr/><i> All is calm!  Looking at this I understand how you thought my entry was not low contrast. To me, lack of shadows (there are certainly none here) and any contrast in lighting is key. But I think low contrast can still include a subject. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree, mine is an extreme example of low contrast. I now added an additional explanation to yours.</td>', 'Originally posted by PennyStreet: All is calm!  Looking at this I understand how you thought my entry was not low contrast. To me, lack of shadows (there are certainly none here) and any contrast in lighting is key. But I think low contrast can still include a subject.   I agree, mine is an extreme example of low contrast. I now added an additional explanation to yours.', '2021-06-09 11:50:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(7695782, 1261938, 30214, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by willem:</b></div><hr/><i> Great viewpoint and impressive trees, but not low contrast in my view. The shapes come out so well exactly because of the contrast between trees and sky. If you look at the histogram you also see a very wide distribution of tones across nearly the total spectrum. In low contrast I would expect a narrow band of tones. I do like the fact that the trees are not all black and still show different tones and detail. </i></td></tr></table> Thank you Willem. Perhaps you''re right and I should have made it even less contrasty (would be very easy to do in p/p). To my defense, there are no black or white tones in this image at all. So it is a low contrast image in my book. Not very low, but low :).</td>', 'Originally posted by willem: Great viewpoint and impressive trees, but not low contrast in my view. The shapes come out so well exactly because of the contrast between trees and sky. If you look at the histogram you also see a very wide distribution of tones across nearly the total spectrum. In low contrast I would expect a narrow band of tones. I do like the fact that the trees are not all black and still show different tones and detail.  Thank you Willem. Perhaps you''re right and I should have made it even less contrasty (would be very easy to do in p/p). To my defense, there are no black or white tones in this image at all. So it is a low contrast image in my book. Not very low, but low :).', '2021-06-09 13:29:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(7695787, 1261745, 50695, '<td valign="top">a lovely way to teach me a new word. thank you!</td>', 'a lovely way to teach me a new word. thank you!', '2021-06-09 15:11:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(7695788, 1261938, 104230, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, a wonderful use of the wide-angle Fisheye Lens. The trees taper so much that I could swear the tops are actually moving in this image. <br/> <br/>After we move we will be surrounded by a different vegetation including much taller trees than typically grow here on Cape Cod, and this will encourage me to include the wide-angle Fisheye when I start capturing our new surroundings.. (we will still be in Massachusetts, but nearer Boston).<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2021-06-09 18:08:41.</i></td>', 'Congratulations, a wonderful use of the wide-angle Fisheye Lens. The trees taper so much that I could swear the tops are actually moving in this image.  After we move we will be surrounded by a different vegetation including much taller trees than typically grow here on Cape Cod, and this will encourage me to include the wide-angle Fisheye when I start capturing our new surroundings.. (we will still be in Massachusetts, but nearer Boston).', '2021-06-09 15:33:29.000000', '2021-06-09 19:08:41.000000', 0),
(7695798, 1261921, 173844, '<td valign="top">One of three co-favorites of the challenge.  It''s marvelous how you''ve portrayed such exhilarating dynamism in a low key image.  The lighthouse itself is the trace that holds fast against the storm.  As almost the incarnation of the force of nature, the sea cloud is a soaring presence.</td>', 'One of three co-favorites of the challenge.  It''s marvelous how you''ve portrayed such exhilarating dynamism in a low key image.  The lighthouse itself is the trace that holds fast against the storm.  As almost the incarnation of the force of nature, the sea cloud is a soaring presence.', '2021-06-09 22:56:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(7695849, 1261672, 173844, '<td valign="top">One of three personal favorites of the challenge.  The modulations of sea, fog, sky and clouds are gorgeous.  The pole and bird are perfect punctuation, seemingly, but not at all necessarily, justification for the whole.  Wouldn''t do poorly in a minimalism challenge.</td>', 'One of three personal favorites of the challenge.  The modulations of sea, fog, sky and clouds are gorgeous.  The pole and bird are perfect punctuation, seemingly, but not at all necessarily, justification for the whole.  Wouldn''t do poorly in a minimalism challenge.', '2021-06-10 18:42:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(7695850, 1261885, 173844, '<td valign="top">One of three personal favorites of the challenge.  You have a way with white, especially how you wrangle the grays into play.  Also, gotta love the sparkle.  Was thinking this is the underside of a mushroom.  Quite lovely.</td>', 'One of three personal favorites of the challenge.  You have a way with white, especially how you wrangle the grays into play.  Also, gotta love the sparkle.  Was thinking this is the underside of a mushroom.  Quite lovely.', '2021-06-10 18:48:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(7695864, 1261938, 122678, '<td valign="top">Congratulations</td>', 'Congratulations', '2021-06-10 23:55:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(7695865, 1261921, 122678, '<td valign="top">Congratulations<br/>Beautiful image</td>', 'CongratulationsBeautiful image', '2021-06-10 23:56:05.000000', NULL, 0),
